Rest operator: 
The Rest operator is a javascript es6 feature , it allows us to collect multiple elements into an array.
it is useful when we donot in advance how many arguments pass to a function.

function func(...numbers){
  let sum = 0;
  for (let num of numbers){
    console.log(num)
    sum += num; 
  }
  return sum;
}
console.log(func(1,2,3,4,5))

Difference between Rest and Spread
Rest	                         Spread
Collects elements	           Expands elements
Used in function parameters	  Used in function calls, arrays       and                               objects
Collects into an array    	Unpacks array elements

Easy way to remember:
- Rest (...) = Collect
- Spread (...) = Expand

Spread operator:
the spread operator is a javascript es6 feature, it allows us to expand the elements in an array.
commonly used for copying,merging,and pass array elements as function arguments.

Rest (...) = Collect
Spread (...) = Expand

Copying an Array:

const original = [1, 2, 3];
const copy = [...original]; 

copy.push(4);
console.log(original); // [1, 2, 3] -> Unaffected
console.log(copy);     // [1, 2, 3, 4]

Merging Arrays:
const fruits = ["apple","banana","guaua"]
const veg = ["carrot","beans"]
const result = [...fruits,...veg]
console.log(result)

Spread operator with objects

vendor = {
    name : "Renuka",
    company : "ITC"
}
updatedvendor = {
    ...vendor,
    location : "bangalore"
}
console.log(updatedvendor)

